  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 316 PM CDT Thu Jun 4 2026\n\nSfc high pressure continues to keep us pleasant even as it shift to \nthe southeast this evening and overnight. Overnight lows will be in \nthe 60s. Tomorrow will be another pleasant day before heat and \nprecip chances start ramping up this weekend into next week. \nSaturday will be warmer in the upper 80s to lower 90s with \nincreasing moisture as dew points reach into the mid to upper 60s.\n\nRain chances come back on Sunday with the greatest chances (70-80%) \nover SEMO and reaching into southern IL and western KY. 50-60% \nchances then spread to area wide by Sunday overnight and ramp up \nfurther to around 70-80% by Monday morning through the afternoon. \nDaily chances then continue through mid to late week ranging from 40-\n50% Tuesday morning to 20-30% chances Wednesday and dampening to 20% \nsporadic chances on Thursday. All told, Sunday through Thursday most \nof the area (with the exception of the Evansville Tri-State) could \nsee 1.5-2.5\" of rainfall with locally higher amounts possible. \n\nWith all this added moisture comes hotter and stickier weather this \nnext week! Highs are in the upper 80s to lower 90s with dewpoints \nin the 70s.",
